{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy","id":1453321,"title":"Full-bloods Can NOT use Thin-blood Alchemy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-23T19:15:47-07:00","id":1453321,"title":"Full-bloods Can NOT use Thin-blood Alchemy","content":"<b>I've recently been watching L.A. By Night and in it the character Eva seems to have learned TBA, I've also done some searching and have seen some people allow non-thin-bloods to learn it. Let me preface this with the obvious &quot;you're game, you're rules&quot; but it is my contention that TBA is an EXCLUSIVLY thin-blood discipline on the bases that it require specifically thin-blood to work, as thin-blood has properties that &quot;thicker-blood&quot; does not have. I will defend this contention:</b><br /> <br /> <i>(pg184) The Duskborn change as they feed. Thin-Blood Alchemy is the mastery of this process.</i><br /> <br /> <b>From this we can see that TBA is an extension of the thin-blood\u2019s ability to \u201cpull\u201d more from the blood they feed on. An ability the full-bloods do not have, at least not to the same functional extent (see below). </b><br /> <br /> <i>(pg228) Drinking blood with intense temperament gives the drinker one additional die for dice pools involving a discipline that corresponds to that Resonance. This bonus lasts until the vampire\u2019s next drink of blood dilutes it, or until the vampire\u2019s system empties of blood when their Hunger reaches 5.</i><br /> <br /> <b>From this we can see that a full-blood merely gets 1 additional die for pools, they must HAVE the discipline and even then they do not get extra dots or powers, they merely get a \u201cboost\u201d to their current powers.</b><br /> <br /> <i>(pg113) Whenever a thin-blood feeds they gain one dot in one Discipline associated with the<br /> Resonance of the blood consumed, together with one level one power in that discipline. If the Resonance is Intense or stronger, they gain an additional dot together with a second power.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T22:52:11-07:00","id":1453329,"title":"","content":"You're absolutely right. I just don't think things like LAbN stick to canon too closely. Note also that a lot of the livestreams play pretty fast and loose with the rules, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T23:11:00-07:00","id":1453331,"title":"","content":"Regarding LA By Night. I figured Eva's use of telekinesis was a throw back to V20 and before when Tremere had the ability to use telekinesis. Her use of lightning would also suggest this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T23:33:39-07:00","id":1453333,"title":"","content":"I agree with all of you.<br /> Most likely Eva is using things from earlier editions of Vampire, not TBA.<br /> That said, Thaumaturgy had more than a few tricks to cheat, as it were, by imitating/emulating powers/abilities they would not otherwise possess. This was done by making a work-around; via a ritual, enchanted item/talisman (or a Fetish), or a combi-power (Thaumaturgy path + Discipline). Or even creating a new, niche path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\ud83d\udd3a\ud83d\udd3a\ud83d\udd3a\ud83d\udd3aPrimarch Anubis\ud83d\udd3a\ud83d\udd3a\ud83d\udd3a\ud83d\udd3a<br /> \ud83d\udd34\ud83d\udd34\ud83d\udd35\ud83d\udd35\u26aa<br /> \u26ab\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab\u26aa\u26aa<br /> \ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32\ud83d\udd32","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26035-primarch_anubis","name":"Primarch_Anubis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T02:53:08-07:00","id":1453338,"title":"","content":"If you really look into what is &quot;alchemy&quot; then really, it doesn't make sense for thin-blood alchemy to exist. Alchemy is about, metaphorically speaking, turning lead into gold Thick blood is magical and divine, thin blood is mortal and mundane. Caine is 1, mortals are 0, and everything between is a decimal place. Caine is methaphorical Gold, mortals are metaphorical lead. Being half and half doesn't shouldn't give you an advantage, purity gives you an advantage. Purity is divinity, or at least, the absolute best state for magic to flourish, whilst thin blood is muddy and mundane, and really a rather terrible state to be in. WoD benefits a lot because it draws from actual esoteric practices and ideas, but this TBA? It's DnD alchemy, or pop-culture alchemy, it's simple potion making, devoid of wider metaphysical conotations, existing only for gameplay/because someone thought it would be cool. To truly be Alchemy, you can't limit it to thinbloods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T05:28:34-07:00","id":1453349,"title":"","content":"I agree that TBA should only be for Thinbloods by the book.<br /> <br /> For my part I find it interesting that in the sorta official showcase game they immediately throw out thaumaturgy as written in book. <br /> <br /> Maybe because TBA feels in some ways more like Thaumaturgy than anything Thinbloods should have? (The ingredients and reasoning are strange, but the effects mostly resemble V20 Thaum)<br /> <br /> Being a thin blood and using alchemy seems surprisingly advantageous for someone that is supposed to be screwed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T08:22:53-07:00","id":1453365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453331#post1453331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding LA By Night. I figured Eva's use of telekinesis was a throw back to V20 and before when Tremere had the ability to use telekinesis. Her use of lightning would also suggest this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you are correct and that actually helps me a lot as far as my head-canon lol thanks man","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T08:32:32-07:00","id":1453366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453338#post1453338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you really look into what is &quot;alchemy&quot; then really, it doesn't make sense for thin-blood alchemy to exist. Alchemy is about, metaphorically speaking, turning lead into gold Thick blood is magical and divine, thin blood is mortal and mundane. Caine is 1, mortals are 0, and everything between is a decimal place. Caine is methaphorical Gold, mortals are metaphorical lead. Being half and half doesn't shouldn't give you an advantage, purity gives you an advantage. Purity is divinity, or at least, the absolute best state for magic to flourish, whilst thin blood is muddy and mundane, and really a rather terrible state to be in. WoD benefits a lot because it draws from actual esoteric practices and ideas, but this TBA? It's DnD alchemy, or pop-culture alchemy, it's simple potion making, devoid of wider metaphysical conotations, existing only for gameplay/because someone thought it would be cool. To truly be Alchemy, you can't limit it to thinbloods.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So I think you are looking at this all wrong, Caine is NOT the metaphorical gold. Caine is the lead, he is cursed by &quot;god&quot;, but in turn, touched by &quot;god&quot;. Or he is touched by &quot;true magick&quot;. However you want to see it. Mortals are the filter for that divine power. They filter away the curse while at the same time reducing the amount of divinity or &quot;pure&quot; power in each generation. But when you get to thin-bloods you start to reach a point where the curse is barley there and the &quot;pure&quot; divinity is able to shine through. Yes it is diluted, but it is able to do things cursed blood is not able to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6922,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","user":"Houston810","date":". 06-24-2021, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T08:44:59-07:00","id":1453367,"title":"","content":"Caine very much is the metaphorical Gold. Being cursed by god is a story, but reaching beyond the 5th &quot;mundane&quot; level that caps off mortals? Getting 6,7,8,9 or 10 dots of an Attribute? That's becoming gold. Each generation is a dilution. Gnostic thought (What the Church of Caine/Followers of Set believe) would hold that Caine is a divine emanation, something that falls from outside of reality as a divine being, gets progressively more earthly and mundane (each gen weaker than the last) and which eventually turns around and needs to shoot up (diablerie) any &quot;curse&quot; aspect is simply the natural reaction of the mundane world reacting to the divine. It's not unique to vampires; Transendent mages with more than 6 dots are also rejected heavily be reality, which is why they spend so much time in the umbra. Just like the philosipher's stone or the panacea, Caine very much is they hypothetical ideal of alchemy, or at least the vampiric path of alchemy. Thin bloods being &quot;more&quot; than regular vampires is just someone wanting to give thinbloods more value, it doesn't align with the metaphysics; thinbloods are weak vampires, but ghouls can't progress as mages, so like an emanation, the thinblood's only choice to reach perfection is to rise up on the path provided for them; they need to eat their way up to be divine, just like other vampires, only for thinbloods the need is more pressing. The advantage of being a thinblood is less curse, less reality rejection not &quot;more powers&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T08:55:15-07:00","id":1453368,"title":"","content":"Thinbloods have access to powers that prior generations don't because they're a synthesis of vampire and human. What I said doesn't mean anything, other than that it's easy to drag words from alchemy into the argument and staple them onto what are really foregone conclusions based on aesthetic preferences. <br /> <br /> I like the idea of prior generations panicking over the thought of Thinblood evolution threatening to leave them behind, and think it's a very authentic take on the human generation gap in real life, but with that said I also believe it's perfectly fine to not want the Thinbloods to have this power for reasons of your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T09:22:58-07:00","id":1453372,"title":"","content":"There are a few great reasons to fear thin-bloods<br /> <br /> 1- Being a reject in both societies means they've got no guidance and they're going to make messy mistakes and probably breach the masquerade. <br /> 2- The cure for thin-blood is Diablerie, and nobody wants to be that cure. <br /> 3- Daywalkers are scary<br /> <br /> but &quot;they're the next step in vampire evolution&quot; sounds like the plot of a B-Movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T09:43:54-07:00","id":1453375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453372#post1453372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but &quot;they're the next step in vampire evolution&quot; sounds like the plot of a B-Movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but it seems like the logical conclusion to me.<br /> <br /> The numbers mushroom, they organise, they make being a Thinblood attractive, they infiltrate human society, they kill most old vampires, they turn themself into a half human aristocracy.<br /> <br /> The hate from normal vampires seems to ensure that they will be hostile and might even help in creating a group identity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26030,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","user":"mfalkenb","date":". 06-24-2021, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T11:41:13-07:00","id":1453385,"title":"","content":"I don't wanna rain on the parade too much, but I don't think that's the logical conclusion at all. <br /> <br /> First, in V5, they're garbage; they don't have disciplines, they still need to sleep for the majority of your average day, they still have to contend with the beast, they still need to feed, and their only plus is that they live a long time. TBA gives them discount disciplines and lets them provide services, but A: most thinbloods aren't going to learn TBA, and it's not like they're going to be exposed to the rituals, and B; They're probably just going to be enslaved by a full-blooded vampire if they ever get to the point of being useful. There's an extra reason to kill them in V5; they join clans when they eat up, which is more reason for them to eat up, and thus more reason to put them down. They're also kinda hopeless at sustainable feeding without disciplines, but I suppose you are going with the aristocratic idea and presume being a thin-blood will attract the rich, which might indeed counter the lack of disciplines. In OG VTM, they're better off, but their hopes of being an undead aristocracy are pretty slim. Firstly, because more than half of them are failed embraces so you're not going to want to volunteer. Second, though they have disciplines, their cap is lower, and they can't blood bond, and they still need to sleep each day. If we're talking about who kills who, the full-bloods have an advantage in either universe. They have better disciplines, numbers, can more easily reproduce, they can blood bond... Really, you'd only want to become a thinblood if you were dying. <br /> <br /> Also full-blooded vampries are of course going to have a much stronger group identity than thinbloods. Their conditions are more extreme, they have clans,..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T11:46:17-07:00","id":1453387,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453367#post1453367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caine very much is the metaphorical Gold. Being cursed by god is a story, but reaching beyond the 5th &quot;mundane&quot; level that caps off mortals? Getting 6,7,8,9 or 10 dots of an Attribute? That's becoming gold. Each generation is a dilution. Gnostic thought (What the Church of Caine/Followers of Set believe) would hold that Caine is a divine emanation, something that falls from outside of reality as a divine being, gets progressively more earthly and mundane (each gen weaker than the last) and which eventually turns around and needs to shoot up (diablerie) any &quot;curse&quot; aspect is simply the natural reaction of the mundane world reacting to the divine. It's not unique to vampires; transcendent mages with more than 6 dots are also rejected heavily by reality, which is why they spend so much time in the umbra. Just like the philosopher's stone or the panacea, Caine very much is the hypothetical ideal of alchemy, or at least the vampiric path of alchemy. Thin bloods being &quot;more&quot; than regular vampires is just someone wanting to give thinbloods more value, it doesn't align with the metaphysics; thinbloods are weak vampires, but ghouls can't progress as mages, so like an emanation, the thinblood's only choice to reach perfection is to rise up on the path provided for them; they need to eat their way up to be divine, just like other vampires, only for thinbloods the need is more pressing. The advantage of being a thinblood is less curse, less reality rejection not &quot;more powers&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You say Cain being cursed by god is just a story, but Cain is just a story. He\u2019s just an idea and as theoretically powerful as a &quot;10dot in everything&quot; Cain figure might be he can literally be hand waved out of existence in a second by true magick. And whatever lore you want to back Cain was created. At this point you are defending a pet theory and not seeing the bigger picture. I\u2019ve seen you around. You\u2019re a natural contrarian, and I respect that. So I\u2019m gonna break it down where we agree, and where I think you are wrong and we can hash it out.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We agree thin-bloods are NOT &quot;more&quot; than regular vampires (but they can be), we agree that they are, and every generation is, a dilution of a lower generation. We agree that the theoretical Cain is the exemplar of \u201cvampirism\u201d.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Here is where you\u2019re wrong: You state that \u201cthin-blood's only choice to reach perfection is to rise up on the path provided for them\u201d and by this you mean the path of diaberizing the \u201cstronger\u201d \u201cmore pure\u201d blood of lower generations. This is incorrect. I\u2019m not exactly sure what your idea of perfection is but Thin-bloods have the potential to surpass most elders in power and side step all of their weakness. They can walk freely in the sun, they don\u2019t frenzy, they have no compulsions or clan curses, they can eat, drink, nap, fuck, piss, shit and live a full life in every aspect of both human and vampire, they can theoretically possess and master EVERY discipline a full-blooded vampire can, and I don\u2019t mean by using TBA. They can theoretically have 10 dots in every attribute all the time. They also have the ability to create brand new disciples. Achieving all this leaves vampirism behind all together. THIS is the only path to perfection. To say otherwise is to say that all the weakness of vampires are somehow not weakness.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now let's tie it back to alchemy, which is an esoteric precursor to modern chemistry and shares MANY properties. Thin-bloods are the result of what\u2019s known as a serial-dilution and then a distillation. The result being a VASTLY weaker product but also a perfectly pure product. You then combine enough of the pure product until you reach the pre-dilution levels. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6922,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","user":"Houston810","date":". 06-24-2021, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T12:38:55-07:00","id":1453392,"title":"","content":"Natural contrarian? Oi, I resent that. My opinions here are generally more popular than those I usually argue against, going by likes at least. I just happen to be a person of conviction... sometimes. <br /> -You'd need a lot of True Magick to hand wave &quot;Caine&quot; out of existence. I'm sure the opposite applies and Caine could Discipline a 10 dot mage out of existence too. <br /> -Thinbloods can't walk freely in the sun. They burn, just less, and IIRC they still need to struggle with staying awake during the day. They do still frenzy, becuase ghouls still frenzy, and Thin bloods are midway between vampire and ghoul, which reminds me that V5 screws that up because Vampires get disciplines, Ghouls get limited disciplines, and thin bloods get... ThBlAl.<br /> -Yes, Alchemy is a precursor to modern chemistry, but we're not talking about thin-blood chemistry, we're talking alchemy. Otherwise the power would be called thin-blood chemistry, and that'd probably be cooler. Alchemy is half magical, and you're doing us a diservice by ignoring that half and going for full chemistry. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> they can theoretically possess and master EVERY discipline a full-blooded vampire can, and I don\u2019t mean by using TBA. They can theoretically have 10 dots in every attribute all the time. </div> </div> </div> Where are you getting this from? </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They also have the ability to create brand new disciplines </span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> This is an ability elders, methuselah and antideluvians also have. </span><br /> <br /> Now, back to thinbloods<br /> The thinblood has two paths; Diablerise up, or become human again (if that's a possibility in your game). Once human again, there are more avenues to divinity, but being an ordinary mortal is the most &quot;lead&quot; state there is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T13:06:27-07:00","id":1453394,"title":"","content":"-Thin-bloods can walk freely in the sun with the day-drinker merit.<br /> -Any vampire can stay awake during the day without struggle with correct influences.<br /> -Thin-bloods do NOT frenzy unless it is induced by magic, same as humans. This is in the thin-blood section of the book. <br /> -I didn't say we were talking about chemistry, I simply referenced it. Everything I mentioned applied functionally to alchemy when it was practiced in the real world. And Alchemy is appropriate given the magical nature of what's happening with TBA. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453367#post1453367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Where are you getting this from?</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-The book... thin-bloods can have discipline affinities and those can be diablerized by other thin-bloods. A thin-blood with day-drinker, life-like, and catenating blood need only make more thin-bloods and eat the ones with the disciplines they want/need (and that's just the short-cut version).</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453367#post1453367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is an ability elders, methuselah and antediluvians also have.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I don't know about elders. Generally just antediluvians and some methuselah under special circumstance, but yes. And that's exactly the point. This is possible because thin-blood is THAT PURE.<br /> <br /> But lets put it to the test. You make the most powerful elder you can with the book. And I'll make a more powerful thin-blood version of it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T13:13:26-07:00","id":1453395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453365#post1453365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think you are correct and that actually helps me a lot as far as my head-canon lol thanks man</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to be of help. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T13:21:14-07:00","id":1453396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453372#post1453372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a few great reasons to fear thin-bloods<br /> but &quot;they're the next step in vampire evolution&quot; sounds like the plot of a B-Movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my own campaign, no one is entirely sure why Thinbloods are supposed to be hunted except Noddist lore says to... But the actual reason its part of Noddist lore is because the Thinblooded can give birth to Dhampirs and one of the Dhampirs (The so-called Last Daughter of Eve) is prophesized to be blessed by God with the power to put an end to the race of vampires. Caine is the firstborn, the Dhampir Last Daughter is the last... Alpha and Omega, Male and Female, the Beginning and the End.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T13:21:14-07:00","id":1453397,"title":"","content":"- I'm not sure &quot;how much&quot; true magick is a lot or if that's even a correct way to talk about it but technically a newly awaken mage could do it day one.<br /> -Thin-bloods with the day-drinker merit can walk freely in the sun.<br /> -Any vampire can stay awaken during the day without struggle given the correct influences.<br /> -Thin-bloods do NOT frenzy, unless otherwise provoked by magic. Same as humans. This is in the thin-blood section of the book.<br /> -I was talking about alchemy. I merely mentioned some alchemically terms and processes that are more easily referenced as chemistry and pointed out the connection. And alchemy is the correct term for what is TBA is given the magical and esoteric aspects of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453367#post1453367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Where are you getting this from?</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> From the book... Thin-bloods get discipline affinities and those disciplines can be diablerized. One needs only make a thin-blood with the day-drinker, life-like, and catenating blood merits, make more thin-bloods and then eat the ones with disciplines you want/need. Train those up to 5, train your attributes up to 5. that's 10.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453367#post1453367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is an ability elders, methuselah and antediluvians also have.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't know about elders, generally it was just <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">antediluvians and some methuselah under special circumstances. But that's exactly the point. This is the case </span>precisely<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> because thin-blood is so pure in the raw creation potential. <br /> <br /> But lets put it to the test. Make the strongest elder you can using the V5 books and I'll make a stronger Thin-Blood ;p </span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T13:26:59-07:00","id":1453398,"title":"","content":"Sorry For the duplicate post. I thought I had lost the original lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T14:22:34-07:00","id":1453482,"title":"","content":"I don't think in terms of evolutionary steps but more in terms of cycles. In a sense most things in WoD loop back onto themselves, and that was true with Thin bloods even before V5. After all the Thin-bloods had inceptor powers just like Caine and low-gen vampires did, and in many ways Caine is like a thin blood/Caitiff himself (less tightly bound to the curse compared to his progenitors but also more 'human' - although in his case its more because he's the genesis of everything whereas the Thin bloods are a result of the vampiric curse weakening in one or more ways.) <br /> <br /> In that same vein I've always seen TBA as a remake of the 'inceptor' ability in a different way and it kinda makes sense. Thin Blood/Duskborn seem to be more of a catch all for all the low-gen and dhampirs put out in ToTB under a single class and the 'original' idea for Dhampir (inasmuch as there is an origin in what little is known in legends and such not influenced by media depictions) have the mortal descendants of a vampire being more prone to sorcery and magical powers. Hence an affinity for TBA would make sense from that view as well. <br /> <br /> To be fair my 'headcanon' for such tends to conflate both V5 and pre-V5 material (time of thin blood and V20) interchangably rather than treat them as distinct, so that could muddy the applicability of the above in discussion since I've always preferred a more nuanced approach to thin bloods than typically depicted (and even V5 leaves out certain details... like it was techncially possible for pre-V5 to have lower generation thin bloods - the lowest gen I've heard the curse weakening to was 6th - but V5 and some latter depictions seem to want to treat them as exclusively high-generation phenomena.) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T17:58:00-07:00","id":1453496,"title":"","content":"Disipline affinity is a thin blood merit and without it you cannot spend xp on disciplines. You can't gain the discipline affinity merit from diablerizing thinbloods. I'm also pretty sure you can't diablerized dots gained through blood resonance because their temporary. I'm not really sure how you expect to gain every discipline as a thin blood diablerizing thinbloods","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T18:24:45-07:00","id":1453499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killtron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453496#post1453496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disipline affinity is a thin blood merit and without it you cannot spend xp on disciplines. You can't gain the discipline affinity merit from diablerizing thinbloods. I'm also pretty sure you can't diablerized dots gained through blood resonance because their temporary. I'm not really sure how you expect to gain every discipline as a thin blood diablerizing thinbloods</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're just wrong. If a thin-blood has a discipline, you gain it from diablerie.<br /> <br /> (pg234) <i>&quot;Every success gives the diablerist 5 experience points to immediately spend on increasing Blood Potency (to a maximum up to the victim\u2019s Blood Potency) or on disciplines known by the victim.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> A thin-blood with a discipline affinity KNOWS that discipline. So a thin-blood would gain it, just like a full-blood would if they diaberlized the exact same thin-blood. If you want to interpret it differently for some reason that's fine, you're table you're rules but its not what the book says.<br /> <br /> P.S. Sorry if any of that came off rude, I'm in a bad mood lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6922,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","user":"Houston810","date":". 06-25-2021, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T19:41:38-07:00","id":1453506,"title":"","content":"Discipline Affinity: You have an affinity for a certain Discipline, picked at character creation. You gain a dot in this Discipline and can learn and retain additional dots in it through experience expenditures, as if you were a normal vampire<br /> <br /> It clearly says you can't retain additional dots without the merit. Maybe you could get 1 dot through diablerie but higher levels don't seem to be permanent since you can't retain them through xp expenditures.<br /> <br /> But it's your table so your rules","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T20:53:24-07:00","id":1453510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killtron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453506#post1453506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Discipline Affinity: You have an affinity for a certain Discipline, picked at character creation. You gain a dot in this Discipline and can learn and retain additional dots in it through experience expenditures, as if you were a normal vampire<br /> <br /> It clearly says you can't retain additional dots without the merit. Maybe you could get 1 dot through diablerie but higher levels don't seem to be permanent since you can't retain them through xp expenditures.<br /> <br /> But it's your table so your rules</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It clearly DOESN'T say that here, but the fact that thin-bloods normally can't retain dots in disciplines is not in dispute here. I agree with you in that regard.<br /> <br /> But what is clear here is that there are some thin-bloods with the ability to retain dots in certain disciplines. They have &quot;known&quot; disciplines &quot;as if they were normal vampires&quot; and per the rules of diablerie those can be taken. And furthermore per the lore it would be strange for it NOT to work this way. One is absorbing the blood and soul of another kindred. This kindred's ability to use said discipline is in that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T21:29:13-07:00","id":1453516,"title":"","content":"Diablerie give you xp and discipline affinity literally says you can't spend xp to permanently learn disciplines without the merit. It doesn't matter that the victim &quot;knows&quot; the discipline because your not a regular vampire, your blood is too weak. If both thinbloods had discipline affinity for the same discipline then could spend the diablerie xp for a permanent dot, because now you are treated as a normal vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T21:57:58-07:00","id":1453518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killtron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453516#post1453516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diablerie give you xp and discipline affinity literally says you can't spend xp to permanently learn disciplines without the merit. It doesn't matter that the victim &quot;knows&quot; the discipline because your not a regular vampire, your blood is too weak. If both thinbloods had discipline affinity for the same discipline then could spend the diablerie xp for a permanent dot, because now you are treated as a normal vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok so, discipline affinity DOESN'T literally say you can't spend xp. It LITERALLY says you CAN. It is stated in the thin-blood section that thin-bloods don't get disciplines. But again, no real disagreement about the idea that thin-bloods normally can't spend exp on disciplines.<br /> <br /> Now I would agree with you if you're assertion that diablerie SIMPLY gives you xp were true, but it isn't. The line is <i>&quot;Every success gives the diablerist 5 experience points to immediately spend on disciplines known by the victim.&quot;</i> It both gives xp and forces its expenditure. A character is actually NOT allowed to NOT spend that xp on blood potency or disciplines. And this is a reflection of absorbing the victim. And it's always been this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6922,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","user":"Houston810","date":". 06-26-2021, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T22:24:31-07:00","id":1453519,"title":"","content":"I stated that you wouldn't learn them permanently. The merit LITERALLY states that they are not permanent. At no point did I say you can't spend the xp. The merit doesn't say you can't spend the xp. So you can gain them but they are temporary because their blood is to weak to retain disciplines","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T23:19:48-07:00","id":1453521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killtron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453519#post1453519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I stated that you wouldn't learn them permanently. The merit LITERALLY states that they are not permanent. At no point did I say you can't spend the xp. The merit doesn't say you can't spend the xp. So you can gain them but they are temporary because their blood is to weak to retain disciplines</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Respectfully the discipline affinity merit states that you can spent xp and that expenditure it is permanent. You have been consistently stating, certain things that you are inferring, are &quot;LITERALLY&quot; being stated when they are not; and that's really bogging this down for me haha.<br /> <br /> Now it is well documented in the book that generally thin-bloods can't spend xp on disciplines. Just to reiterate, this is NOT stated in the discipline affinity merit. What is stated is a specific instance in which the general rule that thin-bloods can't spend xp on disciplines is being replaced by this specific rule. The same is true when the book tells you to spend the xp on disciplines known by victims of diablerie.<br /> <br /> Now, what is known by the victim in this case, what is in the victim's blood, is a permanent discipline. With that said if you want to choose to rule that despite the lore, despite every other instance of diablerie, despite the fact that &quot;thin-blood&quot; actually absorbs MORE readily than full-blood (so much so that there is a whole new discipline build around that fact), that in this specific case that discipline is not fully absorbed... you are free to do so. But it is not consistent with the text in this edition or the pervious editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6922,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","user":"Houston810","date":". 06-26-2021, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T02:29:59-07:00","id":1453529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453385#post1453385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't wanna rain on the parade too much, but I don't think that's the logical conclusion at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>No surprise there. <br /> <br /> In terms of supernatural power fullbloods absolutely have the upper hand - as you point out. On a one to one basis they should whack the thinbloods.<br /> <br /> <br /> It is only my personal interpretation that in the long term brains, organisation and age win out. Vampiric powers can turn into a crutch. Once you have vast organisations battling it out disciplines become less relevant. <br /> <br /> The Thinbloods are not there yet. Not even close.<br /> <br /> I would just expect the pressure cooker to create a highly organised Thinblood organisation somewhere. <br /> <br /> Once they have the organisation , manpower and money to get the ball rolling I think they have the advantage.<br /> <br /> <br /> The degree of infighting an splintering among fullbloods is legendary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T04:25:04-07:00","id":1453534,"title":"","content":"Full vampires have far greater advantages in Organization, simply by virtue of being full-blooded vampries. They can create ghouls and foster blood-bonds; thin bloods cannot. They can access higher level disciplines (or disciplines at all) <br /> <br /> Moreover, fullbloods can reliably create more vampires. Thinbloods can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T05:58:47-07:00","id":1453538,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453534#post1453534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Full vampires have far greater advantages in Organization, simply by virtue of being full-blooded vampries. They can create ghouls and foster blood-bonds; thin bloods cannot. They can access higher level disciplines (or disciplines at all)</div> </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453534#post1453534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Moreover, fullbloods can reliably create more vampires. Thinbloods can't. </span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Full-blooded vampire's upper-hand in organization is based almost entirely on age. On basically getting there first. The simple fact of the matter here is that thin-bloods <i>can</i> foster blood-bonds, all of them <i>can</i> create ghouls, they <i>can</i> reliably create more vampires (tho it was a percentage chance in the previous editions, now it is a merit). And as I feel I have exhaustively shown here lol, they <i>can</i> access disciplines (in many ways).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And all of this is precisely the horror of thin-bloods. On a personal level they are weak, clanless, bullied, hunted, used, and abused, barely vampire shit-bags. But as a population their potential is vast. And this is why the book of nod speaks not of JUST the time of thin-blood, but when thin-bloods and caitiff come to <i>rule</i> the cities.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thin-bloods are, in MANY ways, weaker in this edition starting out, but they have also been given a greater potential in this edition; and that is intentional. If you read the previous editions and compare them, an organization and coming together of thin-bloods and caitiff IS the narrative. That\u2019s story arc, it's being built in the the meta plot with this edition. It kinda always has been the arc.<br /> <br /> I would encourage everyone to read &quot;The Time of Thin-blood&quot; book from the previous edition as it gives a greater context for all of this.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6922,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","user":"Houston810","date":". 06-26-2021, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T06:07:13-07:00","id":1453539,"title":"","content":"1. Ghouls and bloodbonds - yes. It is an advantage. Many vampires use these tools to create henchmen. They never bother to create real organisations. Just a loose network of personal connections. At best you have something akin to warbands, militias or a small feudal levy.<br /> <br /> <b>I would argue that it is precisely because they are so powerful personally that their societal potential seems stunted.</b> Plus Feeding competition. Plus having these powers seems to mess with you psyche.<br /> <br /> Because Thinblood do not have a hammer they are not looking for a nail. One of them will probably invent glue.<br /> <br /> 2. Thin Blood can reliably create recruits. Take a fullblood of high generation and have him embrace. Some die some make it. Repeat<br /> <br /> Maybe deadly mantis vs ant swarm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26030,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","user":"mfalkenb","date":". 06-26-2021, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T08:08:56-07:00","id":1453552,"title":"","content":"If it's a merit, it means it's rare. What are the chances you're going to come across a thinblood who can blood bond and also use disciplines and also... <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26030\" data-vbnamecard=\"26030\">mfalkenb</a> <br /> Nah, the majority of vampire relations aren't due to blood bonds. The ventrue, for instance, are written to be extremely reluctant to fall back on their gifts; Normal persuasion, money, these things have always been preferable for vampires. The blood bond functions more as a security net, making sure the vampire has a few very loyal retainers/allies that won't be poached, and helping vampires get the resources they need initially to get the ball rolling. If you had a vampire and a thinblood, all things being equal, and made a competition to see who could become a millionaire first, the vampire would win. <br /> <br /> Yes, they can reliably create recruits if they rely on a fullblood... do you see the problem with your statement? <br /> <br /> Thinbloods still see one-another as competition. I don't know why you'd think they're not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T09:40:19-07:00","id":1453559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453552#post1453552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If it's a merit, it means it's rare. What are the chances you're going to come across a thinblood who can blood bond and also use disciplines and also\u2026</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dude a merit doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s rare. There are 8 merits and you HAVE to pick 1 and get to pick up to 3. That math is simple, so the answer to you question is: about as often as you roll a 20 in DnD. Happens all the time.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453552#post1453552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, they can reliably create recruits if they rely on a fullblood... do you see the problem with your statement?</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They do not need full-bloods to ghoul or bond\u2026 All thin-bloods can ghoul and bonding is a merit in this edition. This is becoming exhausting lol</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453552#post1453552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinbloods still see one-another as competition. I don't know why you'd think they're not.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The bloodlines kindred were shown as banding together on the beach. The ToTB book depicts them only ever in groups. The V5 book art explicitly shows them helping and embracing each other. The book also talks about how the alchemy skill has built itself up by sharing, building on the work of other cooks. Thin-bloods banding together to a higher degree has ALWAYS been part of the meta-plot. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sir, with respect, this is why I said you are a </span>contrarian<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, the math is clear, the text is clear, and thin-bloods are almost always seen working together to a higher degree. I offer you peace Sir lol</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6922,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","user":"Houston810","date":". 06-26-2021, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T11:47:23-07:00","id":1453579,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dude a merit doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s rare. There are 8 merits and you HAVE to pick 1 and get to pick up to 3. That math is simple, so the answer to you question is: about as often as you roll a 20 in DnD. Happens all the time. </div> </div> </div> Compare how often you roll a D20 in a DnD session to how often vampires embrace. </span><br /> <br /> I considered an in depth reply, but you're also talking about creating an infinite blood scheme in another thread, evidently you're looking to justify cheesing the system, rather than engaging in a productive discussion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They do not need full-bloods to ghoul or bond\u2026 All thin-bloods can ghoul and bonding is a merit in this edition. </div> </div> </div>I was talking about embracing</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is becoming exhausting lol</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> I'm half convinced this is exactly what you wanted. </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I offer you peace Sir lol</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a poor way to offer peace. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T13:50:40-07:00","id":1453590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453579#post1453579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compare how often you roll a D20 in a DnD session to how often vampires embrace. I considered an in depth reply, but you're also talking about creating an infinite blood scheme in another thread, evidently you're looking to justify cheesing the system, rather than engaging in a productive discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>How often vampires embrace is how often vampires embrace. There is no set rate.<br /> <br /> And I wasn't justifying cheesing the system in that post, that was me pointing something out. I was just showing off my math <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Which was incorrect anyway. The whole post was wrong and I was happy for the correction...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453579#post1453579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was talking about embracing</div> </div> </div> </div>Thin-bloods can embrace.... I've pointed this out multiple times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453579#post1453579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is a poor way to offer peace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Respectfully? How do you want it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6922,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","user":"Houston810","date":". 06-26-2021, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T15:50:52-07:00","id":1453726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453482#post1453482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> it was techncially possible for pre-V5 to have lower generation thin bloods - the lowest gen I've heard the curse weakening to was 6th - but V5 and some latter depictions seem to want to treat them as exclusively high-generation </div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know where this 6th gen thinblood is referenced? Lowest I can think of was in the BJD and I belive he was 11th gen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T19:11:02-07:00","id":1453737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy#post1453321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I've recently been watching L.A. By Night and in it the character Eva seems to have learned TBA, I've also done some searching and have seen some people allow non-thin-bloods to learn it. Let me preface this with the obvious &quot;you're game, you're rules&quot; but it is my contention that TBA is an EXCLUSIVLY thin-blood discipline on the bases that it require specifically thin-blood to work, as thin-blood has properties that &quot;thicker-blood&quot; does not have. I will defend this contention:</b><br /> <br /> <i>(pg184) The Duskborn change as they feed. Thin-Blood Alchemy is the mastery of this process.</i><br /> <br /> <b>From this we can see that TBA is an extension of the thin-blood\u2019s ability to \u201cpull\u201d more from the blood they feed on. An ability the full-bloods do not have, at least not to the same functional extent (see below). </b><br /> <br /> <i>(pg228) Drinking blood with intense temperament gives the drinker one additional die for dice pools involving a discipline that corresponds to that Resonance. This bonus lasts until the vampire\u2019s next drink of blood dilutes it, or until the vampire\u2019s system empties of blood when their Hunger reaches 5.</i><br /> <br /> <b>From this we can see that a full-blood merely gets 1 additional die for pools, they must HAVE the discipline and even then they do not get extra dots or powers, they merely get a \u201cboost\u201d to their current powers.</b><br /> <br /> <i>(pg113) Whenever a thin-blood feeds they gain one dot in one Discipline associated with the<br /> Resonance of the blood consumed, together with one level one power in that discipline. If the Resonance is Intense or stronger, they gain an additional dot together with a second power.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Jason Carl has made extensive homebrew, and talked about it as such, for things Eva has like the salve, lighting magic or the Carna fire magic. He also plays very loose with the rules as written, and has forgotten major rules like things for Frenzy rolls. Nothing in LAbN should be used as any litmus test for the rules as written from the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T05:39:37-07:00","id":1453750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killtron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453726#post1453726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you know where this 6th gen thinblood is referenced? Lowest I can think of was in the BJD and I belive he was 11th gen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well I don't know of a specific character, but dusting off my old copy of Dark Ages Vampire (first edition), I see that characters can start at 7th Generation, and the Flaw: Thin-Blooded can be taken by them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T10:24:57-07:00","id":1453762,"title":"","content":"It's one of the Giovanni Chroncile books. I have to dig it out although I may have referenced it in the past. I'll try to get a quote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T18:29:43-07:00","id":1453805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453750#post1453750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well I don't know of a specific character, but dusting off my old copy of Dark Ages Vampire (first edition), I see that characters can start at 7th Generation, and the Flaw: Thin-Blooded can be taken by them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which was superseded by later mechanics, such as the various Thin Blood flaws from later editions and how they listed Generation. This is a further superseding of later mechanics. So it doesn't really apply, or matter, when discussing Teebs of V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T22:53:30-07:00","id":1454798,"title":"","content":"Ugh slow to get back to this. Anyhow I'm not aware of any 'superseding' of mechanics, since DAV Revised and 20th have flaws that simulate thin-blooded-ness after a fashion. They just don't call it that (two flaws specifically - 'cannot embrace' and 'weak blood' which differ from the earlier depictions. Revised at least even treats being 13th gen as a flaw with many of them having one of two previous due to 'thin blood') Mechanically the drawbacks are much different (and severe) than in ToTB or BJD in some ways (For weak blood disciplines are capped at 4 dots in addition to being incapable of embracing or creating ghouls and the double blood point costs. Cannot Embrace seems to be a lesser 'mutation' of the curse but still one all the same.) In modern nights ToTB suggests multiple times (mechnically and narratively) that its possible for lower generations to have thin blood, its just far rarer than it is for the highest generations. They don't flesh this out very well and there's no real mechanical benefit to it (some parts suggest its more 'alternative' rules in fact) but its not expressly forbidden either. Narratively Netchurch says its 'rare' but doesn't call it impossible among lower generations when discussing thin blood syndrome - its just more common among the higher generations particularly the 15th. Beckett's Jyhad Diary (more recent and has the mention of 16th generation) takes a similar tack: low-generation thin bloods are 'technically' possible but in practice it's more prevalent amongst the highest generations and there really is no mechanical benefit to a low-generation thin blood. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killtron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1453726#post1453726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know where this 6th gen thinblood is referenced? Lowest I can think of was in the BJD and I belive he was 11th gen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the delay in getting back to this. It's giovanni Chronicle III. I do need to apologize since my prior wording was less clear than it should have been: the book does not EXPLICITLY call him a thin blood, but the qualities reflect traits we know are tied to thin blooded syndrome (specifically the 'ravaging years' flaw from ToTB) so it seems reasonable to correlate them (although as I said Dark Ages Vampire treats the condition very differently than the modern nights so that also has to be accounted for.) <br /> <br /> Another difference between below and ToTB is that Dunlop is a diablerist (a detail I'd forgotten) and it didn't 'cure' his thin blooded condition... but again this may also reflect different approaches that DAV and 'modern' VTM took to the concept since obviously differences do exist. Still<br /> <br /> With all that said, here's the quote FWIW: <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Giovanni Chronicles III</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">. As Dunlop surveyed a burning village, a hoarfrost chill pierced him. His sons lay unconscious nearby as an old witch cackled at him from the darkness. The woman marveled at the destruction he had caused and gave him a simple choice: instant death, or eternal life and vengeance against his enemies. The decision was obvious.<br /> <br /> When he awoke, the witch woman was gone, but her blood still froze his veins. Dunlop fell back to his keep and Embraced his sons to aid in the castle\u2019s defense.<br /> ...<br /> After his first century, Dunlop realized that he was still aging. The old hag\u2019s blood was polluted and corrupt. Dunlop inherited that curse \u2014 and passed it on to his sons. Years of searching for a cure were fruitless. <br /> ...<br /> Everything falls apart. Life and unlife are both nightmares of decay. You realize this with horror because years pass for you almost as they do for mortals. You were young when you became a vampire, but you have become very old after 900 years. You will be dust within a century.<br /> <br /> You sought cures and potions for your curse. Nothing worked; you broke more than a few charlatans over your knee. Vampire blood slowed down the process, but you needed more to stave off the rot. Then you discovered the Necromancers.<br /> <br /> They say they can arrest your decay and have shown you proof of their powers. You have stopped aging for a full decade now, and perhaps grown a little younger!</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T13:45:40-07:00","id":1454990,"title":"","content":"While I can see both sides of the argument, I do want to ask what should a vampire do if they progress into a Full-Blood as a result of diablerie? Should they lose the knowledge they've gained by effectively making it impossible to do? Should the Storyteller refund any and all EXP spent on Thin-Blood Alchemy? Do note that the only rule in the book about this is on page 180 of the rule book, which many rules lawyers would argue only applies to advantages. This is only a handful of questions this particular statement brings up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T08:33:39-07:00","id":1455028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1454798#post1454798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh slow to get back to this. Anyhow I'm not aware of any 'superseding' of mechanics, since DAV Revised and 20th have flaws that simulate thin-blooded-ness after a fashion. They just don't call it that (two flaws specifically - 'cannot embrace' and 'weak blood' which differ from the earlier depictions. Revised at least even treats being 13th gen as a flaw with many of them having one of two previous due to 'thin blood') Mechanically the drawbacks are much different (and severe) than in ToTB or BJD in some ways (For weak blood disciplines are capped at 4 dots in addition to being incapable of embracing or creating ghouls and the double blood point costs. Cannot Embrace seems to be a lesser 'mutation' of the curse but still one all the same.) In modern nights ToTB suggests multiple times (mechnically and narratively) that its possible for lower generations to have thin blood, its just far rarer than it is for the highest generations. They don't flesh this out very well and there's no real mechanical benefit to it (some parts suggest its more 'alternative' rules in fact) but its not expressly forbidden either. Narratively Netchurch says its 'rare' but doesn't call it impossible among lower generations when discussing thin blood syndrome - its just more common among the higher generations particularly the 15th. Beckett's Jyhad Diary (more recent and has the mention of 16th generation) takes a similar tack: low-generation thin bloods are 'technically' possible but in practice it's more prevalent amongst the highest generations and there really is no mechanical benefit to a low-generation thin blood. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry for the delay in getting back to this. It's giovanni Chronicle III. I do need to apologize since my prior wording was less clear than it should have been: the book does not EXPLICITLY call him a thin blood, but the qualities reflect traits we know are tied to thin blooded syndrome (specifically the 'ravaging years' flaw from ToTB) so it seems reasonable to correlate them (although as I said Dark Ages Vampire treats the condition very differently than the modern nights so that also has to be accounted for.) <br /> <br /> Another difference between below and ToTB is that Dunlop is a diablerist (a detail I'd forgotten) and it didn't 'cure' his thin blooded condition... but again this may also reflect different approaches that DAV and 'modern' VTM took to the concept since obviously differences do exist. Still<br /> <br /> With all that said, here's the quote FWIW: <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>What clan is this character? It also sounds a bit like a Samedi, and given the context (GC), I wonder if there's any relation?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1454990#post1454990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I can see both sides of the argument, I do want to ask what should a vampire do if they progress into a Full-Blood as a result of diablerie? Should they lose the knowledge they've gained by effectively making it impossible to do? Should the Storyteller refund any and all EXP spent on Thin-Blood Alchemy? Do note that the only rule in the book about this is on page 180 of the rule book, which many rules lawyers would argue only applies to advantages. This is only a handful of questions this particular statement brings up.</div> </div> </div> </div>No longer being a Thin Blood might be reward enough. But if you're generous, refunding XP seems a decent enough idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T11:01:10-07:00","id":1455526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1454990#post1454990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I can see both sides of the argument, I do want to ask what should a vampire do if they progress into a Full-Blood as a result of diablerie? Should they lose the knowledge they've gained by effectively making it impossible to do? Should the Storyteller refund any and all EXP spent on Thin-Blood Alchemy? Do note that the only rule in the book about this is on page 180 of the rule book, which many rules lawyers would argue only applies to advantages. This is only a handful of questions this particular statement brings up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that PC would just no longer be a thin-blood, keep all their points in TBA but be unable to use them (or might need to abduct thin-bloods to use it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T12:42:05-07:00","id":1455530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1455526#post1455526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that PC would just no longer be a thin-blood, keep all their points in TBA but be unable to use them (or might need to abduct thin-bloods to use it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem with that is the thinned blood needed usually from the user themselves and not other thin-bloods. So with the user no longer possessing thinned blood they'd have no way to use the ability at all, if we go by this thread in the first place. In addition, TBA can't use other thin-blood's blood to activate it as per RAW itself, it needs the user's blood specifically.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but either side of the table is gonna be annoyed by this solution specifically. As a player, I'd be furious and would likely talk with the ST about it this if this was the situation. Most likely I'd quit that table if this happened. As a Storyteller, this would be a dissatisfying solution that only takes away from a story rather then builds on it. V5 specifically takes a lot of inspiration from Chronicles 2e, a sister line, and in both there is a sanctity of traits, and this solution ignores it blatantly. I would never do this in my game, because I personally think it is a very bad idea.<br /> <br /> If I had to give my opinion, I'd refund the EXP spent on the disipline(s), yes you can have multiple instances of TBA. Not only that, but I'd also allow the new full-blood access to starting disciplines, 2 in one and 1 in another, at least a week or less after the attack. They lose their Thin-Blood Merits and Flaws, but those cost no EXP and have no dots so their loss is actually harmless in the grand scheme of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T02:21:41-07:00","id":1455564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1455530#post1455530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Problem with that is the thinned blood needed usually from the user themselves and not other thin-bloods. So with the user no longer possessing thinned blood they'd have no way to use the ability at all, if we go by this thread in the first place. In addition, TBA can't use other thin-blood's blood to activate it as per RAW itself, it needs the user's blood specifically.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but either side of the table is gonna be annoyed by this solution specifically. As a player, I'd be furious and would likely talk with the ST about it this if this was the situation. Most likely I'd quit that table if this happened. As a Storyteller, this would be a dissatisfying solution that only takes away from a story rather then builds on it. V5 specifically takes a lot of inspiration from Chronicles 2e, a sister line, and in both there is a sanctity of traits, and this solution ignores it blatantly. I would never do this in my game, because I personally think it is a very bad idea.<br /> <br /> If I had to give my opinion, I'd refund the EXP spent on the disipline(s), yes you can have multiple instances of TBA. Not only that, but I'd also allow the new full-blood access to starting disciplines, 2 in one and 1 in another, at least a week or less after the attack. They lose their Thin-Blood Merits and Flaws, but those cost no EXP and have no dots so their loss is actually harmless in the grand scheme of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd refund the XP, too, and give them their starting Disciplines like any other vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T22:21:33-07:00","id":1455595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1455530#post1455530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Problem with that is the thinned blood needed usually from the user themselves and not other thin-bloods. So with the user no longer possessing thinned blood they'd have no way to use the ability at all, if we go by this thread in the first place. In addition, TBA can't use other thin-blood's blood to activate it as per RAW itself, it needs the user's blood specifically.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but either side of the table is gonna be annoyed by this solution specifically. As a player, I'd be furious and would likely talk with the ST about it this if this was the situation. Most likely I'd quit that table if this happened. As a Storyteller, this would be a dissatisfying solution that only takes away from a story rather then builds on it. V5 specifically takes a lot of inspiration from Chronicles 2e, a sister line, and in both there is a sanctity of traits, and this solution ignores it blatantly. I would never do this in my game, because I personally think it is a very bad idea.<br /> <br /> If I had to give my opinion, I'd refund the EXP spent on the disipline(s), yes you can have multiple instances of TBA. Not only that, but I'd also allow the new full-blood access to starting disciplines, 2 in one and 1 in another, at least a week or less after the attack. They lose their Thin-Blood Merits and Flaws, but those cost no EXP and have no dots so their loss is actually harmless in the grand scheme of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree it wouldn't work in most cases, but if they are making the fixed &quot;potions&quot; then it might work. There are examples of some of these &quot;potions&quot; being used on other kindred and mortals so the evidence would suggest it actually is possible in this very specific case. Either way I would never run a world of darkness campaign where I'm refunding exp lol I just wouldn't. That's just no consequences baby town stuff to me. I would absolutely give them disciplines and a predator type and all of that.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what sanctity of traits is, but from the context it sounds like a &quot;conservation of experience&quot; rule which has never been in oWoD or V5. BUT it does sound interesting and I'd love to hear more about it or read more about it. Again that doesn't sound &quot;dark&quot; to me but that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T23:42:29-07:00","id":1455598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1455595#post1455595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree it wouldn't work in most cases, but if they are making the fixed &amp;quot;potions&amp;quot; then it might work. There are examples of some of these &amp;quot;potions&amp;quot; being used on other kindred and mortals so the evidence would suggest it actually is possible in this very specific case. Either way I would never run a world of darkness campaign where I'm refunding exp lol I just wouldn't. That's just no consequences baby town stuff to me. I would absolutely give them disciplines and a predator type and all of that.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what sanctity of traits is, but from the context it sounds like a &amp;quot;conservation of experience&amp;quot; rule which has never been in oWoD or V5. BUT it does sound interesting and I'd love to hear more about it or read more about it. Again that doesn't sound &amp;quot;dark&amp;quot; to me but that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not in pre-V5, but it was ported over from VTR for the current edition, IIRC. It's maybe only mentioned as Sanctity of Merits, though (i.e., if you lose a Merit, you get the points back).<br /> <br /> In V20, I would agree with you, although it's still likely to be a source of confrontation between player and ST (and definitely lends itself to an adversarial GMing style). But in V5, XP is so hard to come by and the rules push a certain degree of balance, so I would refund those XP. <br /> <br /> Perhaps I'd let the player buy up Blood Sorcery as an alternative, because Diablerie already sucks enough that you need to sweeten the deal for Thin Bloods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T23:45:39-07:00","id":1455599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1455595#post1455595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree it wouldn't work in most cases, but if they are making the fixed &amp;quot;potions&amp;quot; then it might work. There are examples of some of these &amp;quot;potions&amp;quot; being used on other kindred and mortals so the evidence would suggest it actually is possible in this very specific case. Either way I would never run a world of darkness campaign where I'm refunding exp lol I just wouldn't. That's just no consequences baby town stuff to me. I would absolutely give them disciplines and a predator type and all of that.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what sanctity of traits is, but from the context it sounds like a &amp;quot;conservation of experience&amp;quot; rule which has never been in oWoD or V5. BUT it does sound interesting and I'd love to hear more about it or read more about it. Again that doesn't sound &amp;quot;dark&amp;quot; to me but that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Official called the Sanctity of Merits in Chronicles of Darkness, it is the rule that basically says if you lose a merit for story reasons you'll get the dot back to put elsewhere. This rule, like many others from Chronicles, made it's way in v5 specifically thanks to the fact advantages, which includes merits and backgrounds, now cost exp. Effectively it says, if you lose a merit or flaw you'll get the value back in the form of dots, the more common method, or exp. It also says that if you get a dot because of story it goes away at the end of that story, UNLESS you spend exp to keep it.<br /> <br /> This rule makes sense, and like I said in earlier post on this same thread it doesn't normally extend to other traits. This is because you can't normally lose dots in anything else after character gen, outside of Humanity and Blood Potency. Yes BP can go down naturally during torpor, but that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> Not refunding EXP when you may need to isn't giving consequences, it's saying the PCs choices don't matter. They choose to dabble in TBA, and then later to become a full-blood. If we go by the logic proposed at the start of this thread, they should lose TBA and get to replace it or get their exp back. If they are forced to keep something they literally can not use, then what is the point of having it on the sheet? It's just a reminder that the choices they make can result in them feeling worthless and trash. This isn't a video game, it's a ttrpg based around what's best for the story. Taking away a player's agency like this specifically takes away from the story, and even creates a disconnect between ST and PCs.<br /> <br /> Now that all said, Humanity doesn't work with this argument. For one thing, Humanity normally shouldn't require you to use EXP to increase in v5. Namely because it's 10 x new level RAW in v5, making it near impossible to buy until you've played for at least a year per RAWs own suggestions. I only bring this up in case someone decided to ask about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T08:41:33-07:00","id":1455616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1455599#post1455599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Official called the Sanctity of Merits in Chronicles of Darkness, it is the rule that basically says if you lose a merit for story reasons you'll get the dot back to put elsewhere. This rule, like many others from Chronicles, made it's way in v5 specifically thanks to the fact advantages, which includes merits and backgrounds, now cost exp. Effectively it says, if you lose a merit or flaw you'll get the value back in the form of dots, the more common method, or exp. It also says that if you get a dot because of story it goes away at the end of that story, UNLESS you spend exp to keep it.<br /> <br /> This rule makes sense, and like I said in earlier post on this same thread it doesn't normally extend to other traits. This is because you can't normally lose dots in anything else after character gen, outside of Humanity and Blood Potency. Yes BP can go down naturally during torpor, but that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> Not refunding EXP when you may need to isn't giving consequences, it's saying the PCs choices don't matter. They choose to dabble in TBA, and then later to become a full-blood. If we go by the logic proposed at the start of this thread, they should lose TBA and get to replace it or get their exp back. If they are forced to keep something they literally can not use, then what is the point of having it on the sheet? It's just a reminder that the choices they make can result in them feeling worthless and trash. This isn't a video game, it's a ttrpg based around what's best for the story. Taking away a player's agency like this specifically takes away from the story, and even creates a disconnect between ST and PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>All true. But also, from a lore POV, Diablerie already sucks and high Blood Potency has a big downside in much more powerful Banes. <br /> <br /> Thematically, Diablerie should be appealing because the setting has always made a big thing of it. If Thin Bloods become worse after Diablerie, what's the point? It shouldn't be Sophie's choice but more of a Faustian bargain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now that all said, Humanity doesn't work with this argument. For one thing, Humanity normally shouldn't require you to use EXP to increase in v5. Namely because it's 10 x new level RAW in v5, making it near impossible to buy until you've played for at least a year per RAWs own suggestions. I only bring this up in case someone decided to ask about it. </div> </div> </div>Tangent alert: I have a house rule for Humanity too. I use the V20 system with one hack: you have temporary points called Morality and when you have a moment of truth, you gain a point. When you reach 10 points, you trade them in for a permanent dot. You cannot purchase Humanity/Path with XP otherwise.<br /> <br /> Moments of truth are basically the same as those described on p.115 of V20DA, but you gain a Morality point or two instead of halving the XP cost for advancement. For big moments of truth, where you do something extraordinary, you might gain a permanent dot instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-26-2021, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T09:16:10-07:00","id":1455617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1455616#post1455616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangent alert: I have a house rule for Humanity too. I use the V20 system with one hack: you have temporary points called Morality and when you have a moment of truth, you gain a point. When you reach 10 points, you trade them in for a permanent dot. You cannot purchase Humanity/Path with XP otherwise.<br /> <br /> Moments of truth are basically the same as those described on p.115 of V20DA, but you gain a Morality point or two instead of halving the XP cost for advancement. For big moments of truth, where you do something extraordinary, you might gain a permanent dot instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stealing this! This is mine now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T10:18:20-07:00","id":1455621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1455617#post1455617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stealing this! This is mine now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go for it! It just struck me that we needed something that rewards continued focus on your Path in RP terms without relying on onerous XP costs. I also really like the Dharma system from KotE but felt that would only work for something like Golconda (it runs in the opposite direction to Paths).<br /> <br /> Then I thought about ringfenced XP, like in Exalted, but that was too fiddly. So I went for something that felt very WW/WoD and just added points to Humanity/Path. You lose all your accrued points if you fail a Degeneration check, naturally, and even if you succeed on your Conscience/Conviction roll, you lose one point unless you crit (5+ successes).<br /> <br /> If you want more detail, take a look at my homebrew WIP here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ny_tu7dul9nDs1JRpZlJWwhH4hwTXp1PXt8eD-5O8Lg/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...t?usp=drivesdk</a><br /> <br /> ETA: And here's my homemade character sheet with boxes for Morality: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qZQ8SpNdO_DOwY9WTiE_50ncXmeg0YUy/view?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qZQ...w?usp=drivesdk</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-26-2021, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T16:52:32-07:00","id":1455683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1455599#post1455599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Official called the Sanctity of Merits in Chronicles of Darkness, it is the rule that basically says if you lose a merit for story reasons you'll get the dot back to put elsewhere. This rule, like many others from Chronicles, made it's way in v5 specifically thanks to the fact advantages, which includes merits and backgrounds, now cost exp. Effectively it says, if you lose a merit or flaw you'll get the value back in the form of dots, the more common method, or exp. It also says that if you get a dot because of story it goes away at the end of that story, UNLESS you spend exp to keep it.<br /> <br /> This rule makes sense, and like I said in earlier post on this same thread it doesn't normally extend to other traits. This is because you can't normally lose dots in anything else after character gen, outside of Humanity and Blood Potency. Yes BP can go down naturally during torpor, but that's besides the point.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I honestly didn't know that this was like an official thing in V5. Can you tell me the page its on so I can read up on it? I mean it doesn't make full sense to me, like if I kill an enemy another one doesn't spawn somewhere or if I loose a resource like a car, something else doesn't fall into my lap. But I should probably read up on it I guess.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1455599#post1455599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not refunding EXP when you may need to isn't giving consequences, it's saying the PCs choices don't matter. They choose to dabble in TBA, and then later to become a full-blood. If we go by the logic proposed at the start of this thread, they should lose TBA and get to replace it or get their exp back. If they are forced to keep something they literally can not use, then what is the point of having it on the sheet? It's just a reminder that the choices they make can result in them feeling worthless and trash. This isn't a video game, it's a ttrpg based around what's best for the story. Taking away a player's agency like this specifically takes away from the story, and even creates a disconnect between ST and PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what logic you're talking about, but if its mine (since I started the thread and you said at the start) then I disagree because they keep their understanding of TBA just loose the ability to use it (unless the the fixed version works). The point of having it on the sheet is that its literally part of that character. I don't really use my psych or bio degree but they're on my wall. And like I said there IS evidence in the V5 book that would suggest a thin-blood turned full-blood could still use TBA given access to thin-blood. Which is a perfectly dark and twisted story route in my mind. And nothing about this would be taking away player agency, exactly the opposite in fact. They choose to commit diablerie. They get everything that comes with that. And no one at MY table would whine about something like that. I personally think what is best for the story is verisimilitude and NOT making sure everyone's super happy with their PC lol I don't know what happy go lucky world of darkness you're running but it ain't mine lol Which is fine, it's all good man, I don't think there is any &quot;logical inconsistency&quot; or malicious STing on my end.<br /> <br /> With that said if it is in the rules, I'll have to read up on that and make some changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6922,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","user":"Houston810","date":". 07-27-2021, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T17:37:31-07:00","id":1455684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1455683#post1455683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I honestly didn't know that this was like an official thing in V5. Can you tell me the page its on so I can read up on it? I mean it doesn't make full sense to me, like if I kill an enemy another one doesn't spawn somewhere or if I loose a resource like a car, something else doesn't fall into my lap. But I should probably read up on it I guess.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Page 180, it's a side bar called <b>Gaining and Losing Advantages</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1455683#post1455683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what logic you're talking about, but if its mine (since I started the thread and you said at the start) then I disagree because they keep their understanding of TBA just loose the ability to use it (unless the the fixed version works). The point of having it on the sheet is that its literally part of that character. I don't really use my psych or bio degree but they're on my wall. And like I said there IS evidence in the V5 book that would suggest a thin-blood turned full-blood could still use TBA given access to thin-blood. Which is a perfectly dark and twisted story route in my mind. And nothing about this would be taking away player agency, exactly the opposite in fact. They choose to commit diablerie. They get everything that comes with that. And no one at MY table would whine about something like that. I personally think what is best for the story is verisimilitude and NOT making sure everyone's super happy with their PC lol I don't know what happy go lucky world of darkness you're running but it ain't mine lol Which is fine, it's all good man, I don't think there is any &quot;logical inconsistency&quot; or malicious STing on my end.<br /> <br /> With that said if it is in the rules, I'll have to read up on that and make some changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree to disagree. I just think if something can't be used it should be on the sheet. It's like how in earlier editions, Mages don't keep their magic on their sheets if they are embraced, they lose it completely because vampires can't do true magic. That said I do partially agree with you on the fact a story should be good, but I also think the players should be satisfied with it. If the players can't do something they have dots in, they 100% won't be satisfied in a normal group. If it's different in your group, cool, but I believe something different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T19:02:53-07:00","id":1455691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1455684#post1455684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Page 180, it's a side bar called <b>Gaining and Losing Advantages</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you Sir. Totally new to me haha. Would you do this with flaws too? I don't know if TBA would fall into this cause I guess its just for advantages but I get the spirit of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T20:01:18-07:00","id":1455695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1453321-full-bloods-can-not-use-thin-blood-alchemy?p=1455691#post1455691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you Sir. Totally new to me haha. Would you do this with flaws too? I don't know if TBA would fall into this cause I guess its just for advantages but I get the spirit of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per RAW, 100% also applies to Flaws. If you lose a flaw, like for example your Stigmata is cured by mythic means or an Enemy is killed, then you'll get another flaw of equal value.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":". 07-28-2021, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-28T00:29:06-07:00","id":1455708,"title":"","content":"Personally, if you lose a Flaw through RP, I'd just allow you to buy it off with XP to commit the change. That way, you don't have to take a replacement Flaw. That seems fitting with the spirit if not the letter of the rules (e.g., how temporary Backgrounds have to be bought to make them permanent).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}